  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Durable Solutions to Support Turkiye&apos;s Earthquake-Affected Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the aim to address vulnerabilities, rebuild disrupted livelihoods, support employment, and revitalize the labour market, IOM proposes to contribute to the provision of means for recovering the economic activities of migrants, refugees, host communities, and the small businesses in which they work, in the earthquake-affected region. More specifically, IOM aims to understand the labour market needs of predominant sectors; strengthen value chains, and support job creation for MSMEs, migrants, refugees, and host communities while also ensuring the quality of life and well-being of working households and finally engaging private sector partnerships to support local production capacities and demand to enable migrants, refugees, and host communities in the earthquake-affected region have the means to recover their economic activities.</narrative>
  </description>
